{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"sections":[],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/digipin"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Digipin is a lightweight, offline-first Swift library for generating and decoding "},{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"DIGIPIN"}]},{"type":"text","text":" codes from geographic coordinates."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"DIGIPIN is a national geo-coded addressing system defined by the Department of Posts, Government of India. It divides the country into uniform grid cells of approximately ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"4m × 4m"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":", assigning each cell a deterministic 10-character alphanumeric code derived purely from latitude and longitude.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"image","identifier":"digipin-social-preview"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"This package focuses on deterministic and repeatable results, operates entirely offline without any network or external dependencies, preserves user privacy by relying solely on coordinate-based computation, and fully complies with the official DIGIPIN specification published in March 2025.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Use-Cases","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Use Cases"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Digipin is suitable for logistics and last-mile delivery systems, address normalization and deduplication workflows, emergency response platforms, fintech KYC and verification flows, and any application that requires precise, offline location identification within India."}]},{"anchor":"Installation","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Installation"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Add Digipin using Swift Package Manager:"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["\/\/ swift-tools-version: 6.2","import PackageDescription","","let package = Package(","    name: \"DigipinSwiftExample\",","    dependencies: [","        .package(","            url: \"https:\/\/github.com\/pranamphd\/digipin-swift.git\",","            from: \"0.1.0\"","        )","    ],","    targets: [","        .executableTarget(","            name: \"DigipinSwiftExample\",","            dependencies: [","                .product(name: \"Digipin\", package: \"digipin-swift\")","            ]","        )","    ]",")"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Import the module in your source code:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import Digipin"]},{"anchor":"Usage","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Usage"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["do {","    let digipin = try encode(","        Location(latitude: 28.622788, longitude: 77.213033)","    )","    print(\"DIGIPIN:\", digipin)","    let location = try decode(\"39J49LL8T4\")","    print(\"Location:\", location)","} catch let error as DigipinError {","    print(\"Error code:\", error)","    print(\"Error description:\", error.localizedDescription)","} catch {","    print(\"Unexpected error:\", error)","}"]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The decoder accepts lowercase input and separator characters (such as ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"-"},{"text":"), and rejects invalid symbols or malformed DIGIPIN strings.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Encoding and decoding operations throw ","type":"text"},{"code":"DigipinError","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" on failure.","type":"text"}]},{"anchor":"Platform-Support","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Platform Support"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Digipin is implemented entirely in Swift, has no platform-specific or system-level dependencies, and can be used on any platform supported by Swift.","type":"text"}]}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/Digipin\/documentation\/Digipin"},"abstract":[{"text":"A Swift implementation of India’s Digital Postal Index Number (DIGIPIN).","type":"text"}],"kind":"symbol","topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Digipin\/documentation\/Digipin\/Location"],"anchor":"Structures","title":"Structures","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Digipin\/documentation\/Digipin\/decode(_:)","doc:\/\/Digipin\/documentation\/Digipin\/encode(_:)"],"anchor":"Functions","title":"Functions","generated":true},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/Digipin\/documentation\/Digipin\/DigipinError"],"anchor":"Enumerations","title":"Enumerations","generated":true}],"metadata":{"modules":[{"name":"Digipin"}],"externalID":"Digipin","title":"Digipin","role":"collection","roleHeading":"Framework","symbolKind":"module"},"references":{"doc://Digipin/documentation/Digipin":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/Digipin\/documentation\/Digipin","url":"\/documentation\/digipin","kind":"symbol","title":"Digipin","type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A Swift implementation of India’s Digital Postal Index Number (DIGIPIN)."}],"role":"collection"},"doc://Digipin/documentation/Digipin/encode(_:)":{"url":"\/documentation\/digipin\/encode(_:)","type":"topic","title":"encode(_:)","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/Digipin\/documentation\/Digipin\/encode(_:)","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Encode geographic coordinates into a canonical DIGIPIN."}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"encode"},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:7Digipin8LocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Location"},{"kind":"text","text":") "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"throws"},{"kind":"text","text":" -> "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"String"}]},"doc://Digipin/documentation/Digipin/DigipinEr